    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "the idea of \"hardcoding\" the overlay into the fabric of existence is exactly what i'm aiming for. \n\nit's strange though, once i start the \"harmonizing\" process, i've noticed that the people around me start to react differently. it's not just that they feel \"heavy,\" it's like they literally don't see the things i'm manifesting at first. like, i'll be looking at a manifestation that feels incredibly solid and present, but to them, it's like i'm just staring at a blank wall or an empty space. it creates this massive disconnect in how we perceive the same shared environment.\n\nis this disconnect a symptom of the \"resolution\" difference i mentioned? like, is my new reality actually stripping away their ability to perceive the higher-density version of the truth? if so, how do i bridge that gap so i don't end up completely untethered from social interaction?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
